// D1470 — `__array_new_default__(n)` at a NON-i32 element. The intrinsic's element kind used to
// be hardcoded to the i32 list; it now reads the destination the checker pinned onto the call.
// The destination is what the annotated face supplies, so the un-annotated face is EXPECTED to
// refuse here: with nothing pinning the hole it defaults to `i32[]`, and the f64 store in the
// proof is then a type error. That asymmetry is the capability, not a gap.
//
// The proof STORES before it reads, because every slot `array.new_default` writes is a zero and
// `0` reads the same off the i32 backing as off the f64 one — a read-only proof passes on the
// miscompile this row exists to catch.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/matrix.py, whose docstring is the spec.
// @@VALUE@@
__array_new_default__(3)
// @@TYPE@@
f64[]
// @@PROOF@@
v[0] = 1.25
print(v[0] + 0.25)
// @@WANT@@
1.5
